cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Women's Career Lifespans in U.S. Entertainment
message: If you use this analysis or its derived tables, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Brian
    family-names: Balzar
abstract: >-
  A reproducible analysis of how screen-acting opportunity changes with
  performer age, and whether the age pattern differs between women-coded and
  men-coded IMDb credit classes in American film and scripted television, with
  a parallel analysis of Billboard Hot 100 solo artists. Distinguishes
  confirmed five-year career interruption from career tapering. Public credits
  measure observed opportunity and do not establish its cause.
keywords:
  - gender and age in entertainment
  - IMDb
  - Billboard Hot 100
  - survival analysis
  - reproducible research
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
